Z||000000||LoW_KeY||12-09-2001||10:39 PM||||Ok well I told my dad I'm all about getting a northstar fiero and he's curious whats the CI on it?<P>I'm kind of curious on this too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||artherd||12-09-2001||10:41 PM||||Mine has '269' stamped on it, heh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Standard||12-09-2001||11:01 PM||||Well, according to GM it's 4.6 liters, right?  That works out to 280 cubic inches.  269 ci would be 4.4 liters.  Of course, GM seems to have a habit of 'upsizing' their engines.  My 2.3l quad 4 actually comes in at about 2.2 liters..<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||12-10-2001||03:27 AM||||Northstar has a (oversquare naturally) 93mm x 84mm bore and stroke (respectively)<P>This equals 4564.83cc, or 278.56cid.<P>So, it rounds to a 4.6L, or 279cid, engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: Still no idea why my intake says 269, and why I belived that was the displacement, must have been all the fumes!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
