Z||000007||GTFiero1||12-10-2001||07:10 PM||||yeah, the northstar has 300hp and 300ft lbs of torque (actually thereare two different modle northstarrs one has 275hp) whish maks it a high performing en gine stock.it doesnt weight much more than the 2.8 so it wont degrade the handleing by any amount. a lot of people are useing N* in a lot of custom cars now due to its reliability and its horse power from the factory. infact some people are converting them to RWD in order to stick them in custom cars<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Nashco||12-10-2001||07:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LoW_KeY:<BR><B>Ok another question   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>isn't the overall performance almost like a 350? told my dad the size and he's like why does everyone want a northstar?<P>He was thinking the car wouldn't go that good with one..<P>-KC</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First, it depends on what 350 you're comparing it to.  Some 350s are completely gutless, some are awe-inspiring...<P>Secondly, the standard USED to be, "There's no replacement for displacement," but that's no longer true.  A better engine design includes better power capabilities.  Add a few more cams, double the valves, use some computers to design everything for maximum potential and VOILA...you have a better motor.<P>Another consideration...this isn't necessarily a tractor engine, it's very light and refined.  Cadillac motors are known for being extremely smooth; that's their specialty, liquid-like power.  Even the old 500 ci Caddy big block I used to have was smoother than our low displacement V6!  Some of this may be in mounting, but you get the point...<P>Lastly..."He was thinking the car wouldn't go that good with one.."  Have you ever drove a Northstar powered Caddy?  If so, did you stomp on the tall pedal towards the right??  The Northstar motor pushes that whale of a car good enough to keep you tucked into that seat...now imagine taking 1500 pounds off of that car, lowering it 6 inches, putting the engine in back, and putting a tight suspension on it.  The Fiero definitely goes well enough with the 350!!!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||LoW_KeY||12-10-2001||08:36 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pHoOl:<BR><B>Dude, if you drop a northstar in, i wanna ride!!!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Works for me.. but I plan on buying a fiero with a northstar in it.. hopefully when 2002 roles around someone will have one for grabs.. hopefully a fastback   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Just dropped the 3.4 in mine not too long ago and she's only sitting with 40,000 on her.<P>Why sell that one when I can have two   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If I could find someone to help me with an engine swap I'd possibly just stick her in the formula and sell the 3.4 or basically give it up for the help in return who knows.. <P>I just know its a disease and it won't stop til I get a northstar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> muwahaha <P>-KC<BR><p>[This message has been edited by LoW_KeY (edited 12-10-2001).]||||reg||1
